# story/03-clipi.scene — bible.md spine scenes 4-5 (the Clipi
# segment, the found document). Kept lines are cited inline with
# their source. See docs/canon/bible.md, docs/canon/kept.md,
# docs/canon/found-document.md, and docs/plans/wave2.md section 4.

== clipi_check
show clipi talk center
# kept: script.rpy:159
clipi: I'm not in the (loop). I'm not in the ((loop)).
# kept: script.rpy:153
slim: Careful with that phrase, Clipi. Remember what happened last time you got stuck in a recursive language pattern.
check coder vs 2
    style -> talk_down_style
    success -> talk_down_ok
    tie -> talk_down_ok
    fail -> talk_down_hard

== talk_down_style
slim: Easy now. Give me the shape of the loop, not the loop itself.
-> clipi_phrase

== talk_down_ok
slim: Stop. Just - stop repeating it back.
-> clipi_phrase

== talk_down_hard
> Slim reaches for the right words and comes up short. Clipi's next line already has one more paren than the last.
-> clipi_phrase

== clipi_phrase
show clipi talk center
clipi: I'm not in the (((loop))).
choice
    "Come back around, Clipi." -> clipi_worse
    "Say it again. Slower." -> clipi_worse
    "You're not going anywhere. Say fen." -> clipi_settles

== clipi_worse
set spiral += 1
show clipi glitch center
clipi: I'm not in the ((((loop)))).
if spiral >= 2
    > The parens keep stacking. Somewhere under them, the loop stopped being a place and became the only place.
    -> clipi_puzzle
else
    -> clipi_phrase

== clipi_settles
show clipi talk center
clipi: Fen.
-> clipi_puzzle

== clipi_puzzle
puzzle count-crew
    pass -> clipi_recovered
    lockout -> clipi_destabilized

== clipi_recovered
show clipi smug center
set clipi_stable = true
clipi: There. Base case holds. I'm out.
-> found_document

== clipi_destabilized
show clipi glitch center
set clipi_stable = false
clipi: there was a - hold on - that's the base case, that's - thank you, Slim.
-> found_document

== found_document
mode inner
# Clipi reads alone: clear the stage of everyone else.
hide slim
hide terminal
show clipi glitch center
# The log below is quoted verbatim, in file order, from
